1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,880
how can you go and on average improve anything

2
00:00:03,880 --> 00:00:06,560
given that you don't know any more than anybody else does?

3
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:08,260
That would seem to be surprising.

4
00:00:09,160 --> 00:00:12,240
All right, anyway, so a general point is this.

5
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:15,080
So just because you're ignorant doesn't mean you're stupid.

6
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:17,000
So if you are uncertain,

7
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,000
you can adopt more general purpose strategies

8
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,640
to take account of all the possible outcomes.

9
00:00:21,640 --> 00:00:22,960
Right, so like with search theory.

10
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:26,240
Yes, you don't know what every possible employer wants,

11
00:00:26,240 --> 00:00:28,520
but you can still form general strategies

12
00:00:28,520 --> 00:00:31,600
about to figure out what in general would people like.

13
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:34,040
So maybe there's some employers that like people

14
00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:37,600
